  journal = {History of Political Thought},
  year = {2010},
  volume = {31},
  number = {1},
  pages = {107--127},
  note = {
  CORE ARGUMENT: Carver argues that the German Ideology as conventionally
  understood -- a unified founding text of historical materialism -- never
  existed as such. The opening chapter "I. Feuerbach" was factitiously
  constructed by Soviet editors to solve the problem posed by Marx's 1859
