  shaped how the manuscripts were received, but this framing is textually
  untenable.

  RELEVANCE: Directly challenges the traditional reading of German Ideology
  as evidence of a unified Marx-Engels historical theory. For any account of
  Engels's philosophy of history, Carver's textual deconstruction raises
  fundamental questions about which texts can legitimately be attributed to
  the collaboration.

  POSITION: Radical anti-Engelsian position that denies the foundational
  status of the German Ideology as a joint text.
  },
  keywords = {German-ideology, Carver, textual-history, joint-authorship, High, INCOMPLETE, no-abstract}
}

